{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 124, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-to-output skip to a cell with no such edge gives a large gain, whereas replacing an existing conv gives little or negative change."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a new 0->3 conv path where none existed helps more than swapping one existing op for another."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 3 absent, removing edge 0 cuts the input off from the output, while a skip on edge 3 would keep a path."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without a direct 0->3 edge, removing edge 5 strips away a main route to the output and hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge with a conv adds capacity and paths, which helps more than replacing another op."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Activating the missing 1->2 edge with a conv adds a new deep path, which helps more than upgrading skip, pool or a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 0 feeds nodes 1 and 2, so restoring it from none re-enables most of the cell and helps more than changing one op to another."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Edge 5 carries more of the output signal when edge 3 is absent, so downgrading its conv to a skip costs more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A s